{"repositoryId":1375123435,"availability":"available","full":"tubban1/fly-eye","name":"fly-eye","description":"FlyEye is a browser experiment and developer kit built around a real, signed Drosophila MaleCNS-derived connectome subgraph.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":105,"forks":2,"created":"2026-09-17T22:08:39Z","updated":"2026-09-18T20:41:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fly.fde.fan","topics":[],"demo":"https://fly.fde.fan/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.673Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.673Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.673Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.673Z","stars":105,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Let a fly brain see your world — and let developers run real connectome-derived circuits.","FlyEye is a browser experiment and developer kit built around a real, signed Drosophila MaleCNS-derived connectome subgraph. It turns camera-derived looming signals into modeled neural input, propagates activity through a compact escape circuit, and exposes the same graph/runtime stack as reusable JavaScript and Python packages.","Scientific boundary: the wiring is connectome-derived; the camera encoder and neural dynamics are models. FlyEye does not claim to reproduce a living fly or biologically exact retinal processing."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tubban1/fly-eye/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fcfee563d8f0a1120c96830e9e2153cf71d550773c556ea46e73eb6d0d91cd22","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.747Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.747Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Let a fly brain see your world — and let developers run real connectome-derived circuits.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tubban1/fly-eye/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"fcfee563d8f0a1120c96830e9e2153cf71d550773c556ea46e73eb6d0d91cd22","sourc